WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:02.640
Cheetah are in a race for survival.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:14.560
There are maybe just 7,000 adult cheetah left in the wild.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.880
I've covered the illegal 
trafficking networks

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.320
draining the Horn of Africa 
of their cheetah.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.520
They also face massive 
habitat loss, and retaliatory

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.480
killings by herders when 
cats prey on their livestock.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.320
I want to find out 
what's being done

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:29.640
to try and rescue 
cheetah from the brink.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.800
How do captive breeding 
programs like this

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.400
help to grow wild 
populations of cheetah?

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.240
It essentially boils
 down to genetics.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:39.560
There is a lack of diversity 

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.560
in the current wild 
populations that we have,

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.800
and we need to put healthy 
genetics back into it.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.920
Part of the phased 're-wilding' 
is that we're starting to 

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.520
disassociate normal captive 
settings around them.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.160
When I open up that crate and a 
cat gets released into a reserve,

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.920
it gives me goosebumps 
every single time.

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:02.320
One of our initial cats, that we re-wilded, her name was Khatu.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:04.400
She's one of our 
success stories, and 

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.640
she's currently on her third 
litter already in the wild.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:18.480
I think she's around, but I will 
use my telemetry to track her.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:19.400
Yeah.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.480
So you have a collar on her?

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.960
She has a collar, yes.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.960
She's here, with a kill.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:33.040
Oh wow I see her!

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:35.040
So the cubs they run away.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.400
It's really rare for the 
cheetah to get six cubs, 

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.360
but this one, she does this 
for the second time now.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:44.720
Cheetah like Khatu and her cubs 

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.680
could be the key to 
ensuring that the fastest&nbsp;

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.440
land animal on earth isn't 
consigned to history.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:52.080
But it must happen 
alongside efforts 

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:55.320
to stop trafficking, 
habitat loss and poaching.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.440
Around the world, big cats 
like lions and tigers 

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:00.840
continue to be traded

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:03.440
and kept captive in 
inhumane conditions,

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.760
but they can be rescued 

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.560
and moved to properly 
managed wildlife sanctuaries.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:13.000
That can mean a journey of thousands of miles.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:17.080
I've just been a great animal 
lover my whole life.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.720
When you're talking 
about Eastern Europe, 

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:23.480
there are no facilities, there 
are no sanctuaries there 

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:24.960
for big cats.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.360
So we've got to bring them out.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.920
I met someone and I moved over 
to Ukraine to be with them.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:33.720
And that is when I got involved

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:37.520
 in the rescue and relocation 
of abused wildlife.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.920
We knew we needed to 
get these cats out.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:47.240
I got on the phone, 
and I called DHL, 

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:50.040
and within days they 
had made a decision

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:51.000
that they could do this.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:56.920
So in total, the cats spent 87 
hours in those travel crates.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.960
The one cat Khaya,

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:03.240
shes been been locked in a 
garage size for three years.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:04.720
Concrete and steel.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:07.040
She's never been 
anywhere else.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.480
And to open that door, 

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:12.440
she doesn't know that she can 
step across that threshold.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:17.600
You'll be surprised how 
quickly they adapt

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:19.720
and they'll just be taken 
care of and loved 

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:25.120
 in the way that we can love them, 
and let them just be lions.

